0,Deori people - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deori_people,"The Deori people are one of the major Sino-Tibetan ethnic groups of the Northeast Indian states of Assam and Arunachal Pradesh. They historically lived in the area of Sadiya, Joidaam, Patkai foothills and in the upper plains or also called as the hinterland of the Brahmaputra Valley.",Deori,Sino-Tibetan
1,Exploring the Folk Musical Tradition of the Deoris of Assam,https://docslib.org/doc/5935504/exploring-the-folk-musical-tradition-of-the-deoris-of-assam,The Deoris belong to the Sino-Tibetan family of Mongoloid stock. They are considered to be one of the communities found in Assam and some parts of Arunachal Pradesh in North- East India. The word Deorimeans the offspring of Gods and Goddesses. The Deori culture is facing danger from the clutches of globalization and striving hard to flourish.,Deori,Sino-Tibetan
